  "title": "PUSH and POP",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "al14-l1",
      "title": "Saving Registers",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "PUSH puts a register pair onto the stack, POP takes it back. PUSH B (305) saves B and C, POP B (301) restores them.",
        "A subroutine that pushes the registers it uses at the start and pops them before RET leaves the caller's registers untouched.",
        "Pops come in the opposite order of the pushes: last in, first out."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "006   ; 000: MVI B",
          "005   ;      5",
          "305   ; 002: PUSH B",
          "006   ; 003: MVI B",
          "143   ;      99",
          "301   ; 005: POP B",
          "170   ; 006: MOV A,B",
          "323   ; 007: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "166   ; 011: HLT"
        ],
        "output": [
          "LEDS ○○○○○●○● = 5"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
