    {
      "id": "al14-l2",
      "title": "Register Pairs",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "The 8080 groups its registers into pairs: BC, DE and HL. PSW is A together with the flags. PUSH and POP always move a whole pair.",
        "PUSH PSW (365) saves A and the flags, POP PSW (361) brings them back.",
        "The pair codes: B 0, D 2, H 4, PSW 6, in the middle octal digit: PUSH is 3 r 5, POP is 3 r 1."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "076   ; 000: MVI A",
          "011   ;      9",
          "365   ; 002: PUSH PSW",
          "076   ; 003: MVI A",
          "000   ;      0",
          "361   ; 005: POP PSW",
          "323   ; 006: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "166   ; 010: HLT"
        ],
        "output": [
          "LEDS ○○○○●○○● = 9"
        ]
      },
